019.steps:
1)Configure a new interface X2 , zone: WAN¡­
2)Edit this interface in IPv6 interface page, select the ip-assignment as DHCPv6, enable PD, connect it to a DHCPv6 server, make sure it can acquire PD from this server;
3)Change PD pool in DHCPv6 server;
4)Click Release button to release acquired PD prefix, then click Renew button to acquire the new PD prefix;
5)Check the related PD AO, it must be updated.
6)Test another scenario, in step 3, set preferred lifetime and valid lifetime as 120s,180s, and wait for T1 time arrived, X2 will generate a "Renew message" and it must update the PD prefix to new one, then do not do step 4, repeat step 5.

020.steps:
1)Configure a new interface X2 , zone: LAN/DMZ/WAN¡­
2)Edit this interface in IPv6 interface page, select the ip-assignment as DHCPv6, enable PD, connect it to a DHCPv6 server, make sure it can acquire PD from this server;
3)Configure a LAN/DMZ interface X3, switch to Advanced tab, click the "add address" button;
4)Click the radio button"Add Downstream IPv6 Address Delegated from DHCP-PD" , choose one of DHCPv6 delegated prefix from the drop-down list(ps: X2 delegated prefix), then set the preferred IPv6 address, set the preferred prefix length, it will generate an IPv6 address with type "PD" and display this address on IPv6 interface page;
5)Change PD pool in DHCPv6 server;
6)Click Release button to release acquired PD prefix, then click Renew button to acquire the new PD prefix;
7)Check the related PD AO, it must be updated;
8)Check the downstream interface X3's IPv6 address, it must be updated according to the new PD prefix.
9)test another scenario: Change PD prefix in DHCPv6 server, in step 5, set shorter prefix preferred lifetime and valid lifetime , e.g. preferred lifetime 120s, valid lifetime 180s, skip step 6, then wait for T1 time arrived, the DUT will generate "renew" message and it should update the PD prefix value, repeat step 7 and step 8.

021.steps:
1)Configure a new interface X2 , zone: LAN/DMZ/WAN¡­
2)Edit this interface in IPv6 interface page, select the ip-assignment as DHCPv6, enable PD, connect it to a DHCPv6 server, make sure it can acquire PD from this server;
3)Change PD pool in DHCPv6 server;
4)Click Release button to release acquired PD prefix, then click Renew button to acquire the new PD prefix;
5)Check the related routes, all related routes must be updated.
6)Test another scenario, in step 3, set preferred lifetime and valid lifetime as 120s,180s, and wait for T1 time arrived, X2 will generate a "Renew message" and it must update the PD prefix to new one, then skip step 4, repeat step 5.
Note: On the DHCPv6 server changing the PDpool may require a restart of server. Step6 can be performed by waiting for the renew message after dhcpv6 server restart to apply the new PD pool

022.steps:
1)Configure a new interface X2 , zone: WAN¡­
2)Edit this interface in IPv6 interface page, select the ip-assignment as DHCPv6, enable PD, connect it to a DHCPv6 server, make sure it can acquire PD from this server;
3)Configure a LAN/DMZ interface X3, switch to Advanced tab, click the "add address" button;
4)Click the radio button"Add Downstream IPv6 Address Delegated from DHCP-PD" , choose one of DHCPv6 delegated prefix from the drop-down list(ps: X2 delegated prefix), then set the preferred IPv6 address, set the preferred prefix length, then check the checkbox"Advertise Subnet Prefix of the IPv6 Address";
5)Enable Router Advertisement of LAN interface X3, connect a PC to X3, and enable packet capture on PC;
6)Change PD pool in DHCPv6 server;
7)Click Release button to release acquired PD prefix, then click Renew button to acquire the new PD prefix;
8)After PD prefix updated, check packets send from X3, it must advertise the its subnet prefix according to the new PD prefix.
9)Test another scenario, in step 5, set preferred lifetime and valid lifetime as 120s,180s, and wait for T1 time arrived, X2 will generate a "Renew message" and it must update the PD prefix to new one, then skip step 7, repeat step 8.

